Article 1 Where a party concludes a contract with death as the condition for payment of insurance money, according to the provisions of Article 34 of the Insurance Law, the "consent and ratification of the insured to the insured amount" may be in written form, oral form, or other forms; it may be made at the time of conclusion of the contract, or ratified after the conclusion of the contract.
Where any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be determined that the insured agreed that the applicant would conclude an insurance contract for him or her and ratified the insured amount:
(1) The insured knew that another person signed on his or her behalf to express consent and did not raise any objection;
(2) The insured agreed to the beneficiary designated by the applicant;
(3) Other circumstances where there is sufficient evidence to establish that the insured agreed that the applicant would insure him or her.

Article 9 Where the applicant designates a beneficiary without the consent of the insured, the People's Court shall determine that the designation is invalid.
Where the parties have a dispute over the beneficiary stipulated in the insurance contract, unless the applicant and the insured have otherwise agreed outside the insurance contract, the matter shall be handled separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where the beneficiary is stipulated as "statutory" or "statutory successors", the statutory successors prescribed by the Civil Code shall be the beneficiaries;
(2) Where the beneficiary is stipulated only by identity relationship, and the applicant and the insured are the same person, the beneficiary shall be determined according to the identity relationship with the insured at the time of the occurrence of the insured event; where the applicant and the insured are different persons, the beneficiary shall be determined according to the identity relationship with the insured at the time of the conclusion of the insurance contract;
(3) Where the stipulated beneficiary includes both name and identity relationship, and the identity relationship changes at the time of the occurrence of the insured event, it shall be determined that no beneficiary has been designated.

Article 12 Where the applicant or the insured designates several persons as beneficiaries, and some beneficiaries die, waive the right to benefits, or lose the right to benefits according to law before the occurrence of the insured event, the benefit share to which such beneficiaries would have been entitled shall be handled in accordance with the provisions of the insurance contract; where the insurance contract has no agreement or the agreement is unclear, the benefit share to which such beneficiaries would have been entitled shall be handled separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where the order of benefits and the benefit shares are not agreed upon, the share shall be equally enjoyed by the other beneficiaries;
(2) Where the order of benefits is not agreed upon but the benefit shares are agreed upon, the share shall be enjoyed by the other beneficiaries in proportion to their respective shares;
(3) Where the order of benefits is agreed upon but the benefit shares are not agreed upon, the share shall be equally enjoyed by the other beneficiaries in the same order; where there is no other beneficiary in the same order, the share shall be equally enjoyed by the beneficiaries in the next order;
(4) Where the order of benefits and the benefit shares are agreed upon, the share shall be enjoyed by the other beneficiaries in the same order in proportion to their respective shares; where there is no other beneficiary in the same order, the share shall be enjoyed by the beneficiaries in the next order in proportion to their respective shares.
